  The v7 lifecycle, merged
  This is the synthesis's merge, not any one review's design. The order comes from A (eligible, prepare, obligations, publish) and B (publish last, all or nothing). The plan argument comes from D, the runner as requests from D, obligations with a sync or defer
  

flowchart TB
  IN["inputs + params"] --> NE["needs: analysis queries"]
  NE --> DE["decide: an untrusted plan (D)"]
  DE --> EL{"eligible? (A, D legal)"}
  EL -- "no / unknown" --> RF["refused, with reason"]
  EL -- "yes, witness" --> PR["prepare on a private stagewrites the derivation (C, D)"]
  PR -- "same revision" --> UC["unchanged"]
  PR --> AU["audit: writes, diff covered by derivation (C)"]
  AU --> OB["obligations: sync now, deferred batched (C)"]
  OB -- "deferred" --> PE["pending: settle later"]
  PE --> OB
  OB -- "refuted" --> RJ["rejected, counterexample"]
  OB -- "executor failed" --> UA["unavailable"]
  OB -- "supported" --> PO{"policy acceptsrelation x method x scope?"}
  PO -- "no" --> RJ
  PO -- "yes" --> PU["publish all outputs or none (B)"]
  PU -- "heads moved" --> ST["stale: retry from inputs"]
  PU --> AC["accepted, with receipt (A)"]

  
